=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: `if: false` on a step that installs pytest disables no suite
origin: issue #196 ruling 191.5 — an install command names the runner without running it, so its step is
origin2: not a runner site. v0.5.0 blocked this diff as "pip install pytest-xdist is disabled". The suite
origin3: still runs in the next step.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pip install pytest-xdist
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pip install pytest-xdist
        if: false
      - run: pytest
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
